/-!
# Completed differentials over pth-power formal parameters

Source: EGA IV-1, 0_IV Lemma 21.9.4; ILO IV 2.1.6, before equation (2.b)
(blueprint: lem-per-pth-power-series-completed-differential-comparison).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace KaehlerDifferential

/-- For a finite local algebra over a characteristic-p formal power series ring, the
completed differential kills the pth-power parameter subring and identifies the relative
Kähler differentials over that subring with the completed differentials over the field.

The given algebra structure represents the map `u`. Its scalar tower expresses that `u`
is an F-algebra map. Continuity is the ideal-power criterion at zero for the two adic
topologies. The maximal ideal of `MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F` is the parameter ideal.
The subring B₁ is the range of `MvPowerSeries.expand p hp`: this changes each exponent
vector e to p e and leaves all coefficients in F unchanged, even when F is imperfect.
Its action on C is the induced action through its inclusion in the power series ring.
The equation on every `D c` specifies the equivalence as the canonical comparison.

Source: EGA IV-1, 0_IV Lemma 21.9.4 (module-finite case); ILO IV 2.1.6,
before equation (2.b)
(blueprint: lem-per-pth-power-series-completed-differential-comparison).

Proof:
1. Finiteness over B implies that the residue field of C is finite over F. Apply
   lem-per-completed-differential-finite-conormal: the completed differentials are finite,
   generated by the completed exact differentials, and represent derivations into finite
   complete C-modules.
2. B is finite free over B₁ on monomials with all exponents less than p. Thus C is
   finite over B₁, and its relative differentials are a finite C-module. They are complete
   by lem-weil-pbc-finite-module-complete-over-complete-noetherian.
3. The completed derivation kills F and every u(Tᵢ)^p, hence the polynomial subring
   F[T₁^p,...,Tᵣ^p]. Approximate any element of B₁ by these polynomials modulo arbitrary
   parameter powers. Locality takes the remainders into powers of the maximal ideal of C.
   Leibniz gives d(m^N) contained in m^(N-1) times the completed differentials.
   Separatedness of the completion therefore shows that d kills all of B₁.
4. Universality of ordinary relative differentials gives the forward comparison.
   The relative differential is an F-derivation into a finite complete C-module, so the
   completed universal property in step 1 gives the reverse comparison.
5. Both composites fix every exact differential. These generate the ordinary relative
   differentials by their construction, and the completed differentials by step 1.
   The comparisons are therefore inverses, with the stated generator normalization. -/
theorem pth_power_series_completed_differential_comparison
    (F : Type u) [Field F] (p : ℕ) (hp : p ≠ 0) [CharP F p] (r : ℕ)
    (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [Algebra F C] [IsLocalRing C] [IsNoetherianRing C]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) C]
    [Algebra (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C]
    [IsScalarTower F (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C)]
    [Module.Finite (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C]
    (hcont : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ N : ℕ,
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) ^ N ≤
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C ^ n).comap
          (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C)) :
    (∀ b : (MvPowerSeries.expand (σ := Fin r) (R := F) p hp).range,
      AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) (KaehlerDifferential F C)
        (D F C (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) F) C b)) = 0) ∧
    ∃ e : KaehlerDifferential
        (MvPowerSeries.expand (σ := Fin r) (R := F) p hp).range C ≃ₗ[C]
        AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) (KaehlerDifferential F C),
      ∀ c : C,
        e (D (MvPowerSeries.expand (σ := Fin r) (R := F) p hp).range C c) =
          AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) (KaehlerDifferential F C)
            (D F C c) := by
  sorry

end KaehlerDifferential
